      "check": "Viewed at 1x and 3x nearest on #172336 (beside the exact Ready baseline as the comparison method), the running loop and each individual frame read as ongoing activity and not as completion: no frame forms a check mark or another success-like terminal pose. Expert guidance, scoped to this branch: avoid frames that read as the static symbol of another member (for example the preserved Start arrowhead or paired pause bars); the binding distinction against the delivered Retry and Paused marks is judged in provenance-correction.delivery.q.distinction. For reduced motion, frame zero shown alone with its Working label must read as the stationary Working indicator, distinct from Ready and Paused; the frame choice is this specialist's proposal, not an owner-prescribed motif.",
      "domain": "visual",
      "mode": "visual",
      "status": "unperformed",
      "verdict": null
    },
    {
      "id": "provenance-correction.working.q.motion-continuity",
      "name": "motion-continuity",
      "check": "Normal motion only: play all four existing Working frames at 100 ms per frame at 1x and 3x on #172336 including fourth-to-first wrap; required outcome is one continuous activity loop without a visible discontinuity at the wrap. Stable center/anchor and visual volume are scoped expert quality checks from the Working contract. Evenly paced angular motion/no near-hold is the specialist's chosen quality criterion for this exact reused rotating-segment design, not an owner requirement; a different expressive timing design could satisfy the brief after review. No universal fixed cluster-count/no-morph recipe is imposed. Reduced motion is evaluated separately as stationary frame zero.",
